		<article class="max-w-4xl space-y-8 font-sans border-t border-mapa-contour pt-10">
			<section>
				<h2 class="font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-3">
					How Metro Manila Train Wait Estimation and Headway Cadence Work
				</h2>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/85 leading-relaxed mb-3">
					Unlike transit authorities in Singapore, Tokyo, or London that publish open GTFS Realtime feeds every few seconds, Metro Manila rail operators currently run closed signaling systems without public API endpoints. Neither DOTr MRT-3, Light Rail Manila Corporation (LRMC) for LRT-1, nor LRTA for LRT-2 streams automated train telemetry directly to third-party commuter websites. When a transit app in the Philippines displays an estimated wait time on its own, that figure comes from deterministic schedule intervals rather than transponder hardware mounted inside the trainset.
				</p>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/85 leading-relaxed">
					Train Arrival PH is transparent about how these numbers work. Using published terminal departure schedules, weekday versus weekend timetable extensions, peak versus off-peak dispatch cadences, and exact kilometer post offsets across all 51 stations, the calculator projects the next three arriving trains in each direction. Rather than showing vague averages, the directional cards list the immediate next trip alongside the second and third following trips so you can judge whether to board a packed trainset or wait 4 to 6 minutes for the next car.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-3">
					How Opt-In GPS Station Snapping Works Without Storing Your Location
				</h2>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/85 leading-relaxed mb-3">
					Pressing the Use My GPS button lets commuters snap straight to their current platform without scrolling through 51 station names during rush hour. Your browser requests device coordinates strictly inside client-side memory and runs a Haversine distance check against the known coordinates of every MRT-3, LRT-1, and LRT-2 platform. If your phone is within 650 meters of a station entrance or viaduct, the estimator locks onto that station automatically.
				</p>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/85 leading-relaxed">
					Privacy remains enforced by design: your raw latitude and longitude never leave your browser and are never transmitted or written to any external logging service or database table. If your device is farther than 650 meters from any rail station, GPS auto-snap reports your nearest rail station distance without forcing a wrong selection.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-3">
					Peak Rush Hours, Skip-Stop Mechanics, and Evening Gate Cutoffs
				</h2>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/85 leading-relaxed mb-3">
					Headways across Metro Manila shift substantially between peak weekday commuter windows, midday off-peak runs, and weekend operations because each rail operator deploys a fixed active trainset pool. During weekday morning rush hours (6:00 AM to 9:00 AM) and evening rush hours (5:00 PM to 8:00 PM), LRMC LRT-1 deploys 24 to 30 trainsets across its 25-station stretch at 3.5 to 5 minute headways (scaling down to roughly 18 trainsets off-peak), DOTr MRT-3 runs 18 to 21 three-car trainsets at 4 to 6 minute headways, and LRTA LRT-2 operates with a smaller active fleet of 8 to 10 trainsets (typically 8 to 9 deployed during routine maintenance) at 12 to 15 minute intervals. During off-peak midday hours and weekends, lines withdraw surplus sets for depot checks and space headways slightly wider depending on commuter demand.
				</p>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/85 leading-relaxed mb-3">
					To separate real commuter sightings from timetable math, Train Arrival PH supports anonymous live rider check-ins alongside a Show Est. Trains toggle in the map toolbar. Tapping a live train sighting button broadcasts a solid green LIVE marker projected along the track for 15 minutes; turning Show Est. Trains off hides all simulated dashed EST chevrons so only live rider-tracked trains appear on the map and diagram.
				</p>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/85 leading-relaxed">
					Commuters catching late evening transfers should always check station passing windows carefully rather than relying only on origin terminal times. For example, although the extended weekday MRT-3 schedule dispatches its final northbound train from Taft Avenue at 11:09 PM, that train takes nearly 30 minutes to reach Cubao or Quezon Avenue, while southbound trains departing North Avenue leave earlier at 10:30 PM. Concourse ticket gates close approximately 5 minutes prior to the final train arrival in each direction so station staff can sweep platforms safely.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-3">
					Using the Transfer Cutoff Buffer Checker Across Cubao, Recto, and Taft Ave
				</h2>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/85 leading-relaxed mb-3">
					Because LRT-2 closes earlier than both MRT-3 and LRT-1 (final trains leave Antipolo at 9:00 PM daily, and Recto at 9:30 PM on weekdays or 9:00 PM on weekends), travelers heading home past 9:15 PM through Araneta Center-Cubao or Doroteo Jose often misjudge their transfer buffer. A passenger boarding MRT-3 at Ayala at 9:15 PM will arrive at Cubao around 9:35 PM, too late for the final westbound LRT-2 trip toward Recto and barely catching or missing late eastbound trips passing through Cubao toward Marikina-Pasig and Antipolo.
				</p>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/85 leading-relaxed">
					Similarly, commuters transferring at EDSA Taft (southbound MRT-3 into LRT-1 toward PITX and Dr. Santos) need an extra 5 minutes to walk the elevated covered footbridge and tap in at the LRT-1 gates. The Trip and Transfer Cutoff Checker above automatically adds realistic footbridge transfer time (5 minutes at Doroteo Jose or Taft, 6 minutes at Araneta Center-Cubao) and warns you in advance whenever connecting lines are tight or closed. If your connecting train has departed, the 24/7 EDSA Carousel busway directly beneath MRT-3 continues serving Monumento through PITX overnight.
				</p>
			</section>

